# Canonical author identities for this repository.
#
# git reads this file for `git shortlog`, `git log --use-mailmap`, `git blame`
# and anything built on them, so one person committing under several addresses
# or spellings counts once instead of several times. It rewrites what those
# commands DISPLAY; it never rewrites history.
#
# Format: <canonical@email> <address-seen-in-history> (email only: the
# committed name is shown as committed)
# One line per historical address. Adding an address here is the fix when a new
# machine or a GitHub web edit commits under a different one.

<backroadcreativeco@gmail.com> <joepetjr@gmail.com>
<backroadcreativeco@gmail.com> <joepetjr@users.noreply.github.com>
<backroadcreativeco@gmail.com> <info@backroadcreative.com>

# Bot identities are deliberately NOT mapped. Buddy was an agent that wrote its
# own commits here (see the /work/ ledger); folding its authorship into a human
# would erase exactly the record this repository keeps on purpose.
